{
  "$comment": "Al-Razi School website registrations, imported by `php artisan alrazi:sync-website` from the website's export (never submitted here). Import with: php artisan form:import 14 database/forms/alrazi-website-registration.json. It MUST stay switched off (is_active false) with confirmationEmail false and no notifyEmails: the sync refuses to write into a form that is live or that would email families, because the website already emailed them when they applied. Every value is the website's own, stored verbatim: grade and program are text, not options, so nothing here can drift from the site's list. The student's SSN and the SSN card are never imported, and the insurance policy number only when ALRAZI_EXPORT_INCLUDE_INSURANCE is true. Payment fields prefixed `website` are the SITE's Stripe state, for reference; they never touch Manara's own payment columns. Imported rows cannot be deleted from the admin, only cancelled, or the next run would write them back. A row the website stops returning is marked in `websiteRemoved` (never deleted by the sync); `php artisan alrazi:purge-website-removed` deletes marked rows. A document removed or replaced on the website is removed or replaced here. Each document slot has a `…Status` text field (why a document on the website is not importable here) and a `…Ref` text field (a SHA-256 of the website's storage path, never the path).",
